version: 1.0.0
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Wendinkonte/realistic-well-log-imputation-benchmark
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and reproducibility package for a benchmark of eleven
  well-log imputation methods across four missingness regimes, evaluated under a strict
  leakage-controlled leave-one-well-out protocol on 19 Paris Basin geothermal wells.
  The package contains the data pipeline, the four masking-scenario generators
  (single, block, profile and the realistic multi-log partial blackout), tabular,
  sequential and spatial graph imputers, the evaluation harness with fold-local scaling
  and identical evaluation masks across methods, pooled metric aggregation, the
  significance testing and cluster bootstrap, and both spatial-leakage experiments.
  The well-log data themselves are proprietary and are not redistributed; the derived
  statistics and aggregate results are released.
keywords:
  - well-log imputation
  - missing data
  - partial blackout
  - missing not at random
  - data leakage
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark
  - graph neural networks
  - geothermal
  - Paris Basin
